message.content:
Use the CSS **`:hover`** pseudo-class to change the `span` color when the mouse is over it.[6][8]

```html
<span class="hover-text">Hover me</span>
```

```css
.hover-text {
  color: black;
}

.hover-text:hover {
  color: red;
}
```

If you want the text to change color *and* animate smoothly, add a transition:[6]

```css
.hover-text {
  color: black;
  transition: color 0.3s ease;
}

.hover-text:hover {
  color: red;
}
```

If the `span` does not seem to respond, check whether another rule is overriding it; in some cases, inline styles or more specific selectors can prevent the hover style from applying.[1][6]

